WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.128
HKDSE 2026, Paper 1, Question 8. Topic: HKDSE 2026 · Paper 1 · Question 8 Similar Triangles & Congruence (SAS). This is the full worked solution in English.

2
00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:21.715
In Figure 1, ABC is a triangle. D is a point lying on AB.

3
00:00:21.875 --> 00:00:35.517
Let E and F be points lying on CB produced and CD produced respectively such that BD over over EF and BC equals EF. It is given that BD equals 8 cm and BE equals 6 cm.

4
00:00:35.677 --> 00:00:47.964
(a) By considering a pair of similar triangles, find the length of BC. (b) Suppose that AD equals 10 cm. Prove that triangle ABC is congruent to triangle CEF.

5
00:00:48.384 --> 00:00:53.748
Step 1 times Identify similar triangles.

6
00:00:53.908 --> 00:01:03.117
Key rule: Similar Triangles (AAA). DB over over FE which gives triangle CDB is similar to triangle CFE.

7
00:01:03.277 --> 00:01:10.153
DB joins points on CF and CE and is parallel to FE, so corresponding angles are equal.

8
00:01:10.313 --> 00:01:22.211
Let BC equals x. Since E lies on CB produced, C, B, E are collinear; since F lies on CD produced, C, D, F are collinear.

9
00:01:22.371 --> 00:01:35.132
In triangle CFE, the segment DB joins points on CF and CE, and DB over over FE, so triangle CDB is similar to triangle CFE (corresponding angles equal, e.g.

10
00:01:35.292 --> 00:01:39.079
angle CDB equals angle CFE).

11
00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:44.651
Step 2 times Use the ratio of sides.

12
00:01:44.811 --> 00:02:00.553
Key rule: Ratio of Corresponding Sides. CB over CE equals DB over FE. x over x plus 6 equals 8 over x gives x squared minus 8x minus 48 equals 0, so x equals 12.

13
00:02:00.713 --> 00:02:13.179
CB over CE equals DB over FE which gives x over x plus 6 equals 8 over x (because EF equals BC equals x and CE equals CB plus BE equals x plus 6).

14
00:02:13.339 --> 00:02:28.187
Hence x squared equals 8(x plus 6) which gives x squared minus 8x minus 48 equals 0 which gives (x minus 12)(x plus 4) equals 0 Since x is greater than 0: BC equals 12 cm.

15
00:02:28.607 --> 00:02:35.115
Step 3 times Part (b) — gather the SAS ingredients.

16
00:02:35.275 --> 00:02:51.091
Side 1: AB equals AD plus DB equals 10 plus 8 equals 18 and CE equals CB plus BE equals 12 plus 6 equals 18, so AB equals CE Side 2: given BC equals EF (both equals 12).

17
00:02:51.511 --> 00:02:56.026
Step 4 times The included angle.

18
00:02:56.186 --> 00:03:07.709
Since BD over over EF and CBE is a straight line, corresponding angles give angle DBC equals angle FEC and since D lies on AB, ray BD is ray BA.

19
00:03:07.869 --> 00:03:18.186
so angle ABC equals angle DBC. Therefore angle ABC equals angle CEF which is the included angle between the two pairs of equal sides.

20
00:03:18.606 --> 00:03:23.192
Step 5 times Conclusion.

21
00:03:23.352 --> 00:03:36.549
In triangle ABC and triangle CEF: AB equals CE, angle ABC equals angle CEF, BC equals EF therefore triangle ABC is congruent to triangle CEF (SAS).

22
00:03:36.969 --> 00:03:46.511
So the answer is: (a) BC equals 12 cm (b) triangle ABC is congruent to triangle CEF proved by SAS.

23
00:03:46.931 --> 00:03:55.668
That completes HKDSE 2026 Paper 1 Question 8. Every step shown here matches the worked solution on the page.
